{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('plan-recovery-outcome.json'))\np['description']+=\\\" A third property follows the recoverer's Commit broadcast: it is delivered to the already-committed replica and to a third replica that never saw the instance, and the property asserts that all three replicas then hold the same committed command for the instance.\\\"\np['monitors'].append({\\\"id\\\":\\\"M3-commit-propagation\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH3-commit-propagation\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"commit_propagation_divergence\\\",\n \\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB2-prepare-resolution\\\"],\n \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB2-prepare-resolution\\\"],\n  \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event records the committed command held by each replica after the recovery's Commit broadcast, so it tests whether the disagreement produced by the resolution survives propagation. The binding is the resolution that produced the vector being propagated.\\\",\n  \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The recoverer committed the instance and the Commit reached the other two replicas.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"committed_reply.instance\\\"}],\n \\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"committed_reply\\\"})\np['observable_properties'].append({\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH3-commit-propagation\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\n \\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"commit_propagation_divergence\\\"},\n \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"all_committed_match\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n \\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"instance\\\"],\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"After the recovery's commit broadcast, every replica that holds the instance committed must hold the same committed command.\\\"})\np['uncertainties'].append(\\\"The third property observes the records the handlers hold after the broadcast; it does not execute the state machines, so the applied-state consequence is left open.\\\")\njson.dump(p,open('plan-recovery-divergence.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Same unit and obligation, one further bounded observation: the harness now also delivers the recoverer's Commit broadcast to the already-committed replica and to a third replica that never saw the instance, and the plan adds a property that all three must hold the same committed command. This tests whether the disagreement produced by the non-adopting resolution survives propagation rather than being repaired by the commit broadcast. The local construction run shows replica 0 NOOP, replica 1 PUT and replica 2 NOOP, i.e. two different committed commands for one instance across the cluster; the formal observation is left to the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review.\\\",\n \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"unit-C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-recovery-divergence.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_recvbal_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{}}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-check4.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-check4.json 2>&1 | head -12\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progres