{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission-check4.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn 17 added one further bounded observation to the confirmed recovery finding: whether the disagreement survives the commit broadcast.\\n\\nState on entry. The corrected artifact (8c65f177…) and its review are recorded; the earlier artifact 6a3e98cc… is confirmed in scope for the adoption defect. The remaining limitation I registered was that the recoverer's Commit propagation to other replicas was not driven.\\n\\nWhat was added. The harness now keeps a third replica that never saw the instance, lets the recoverer's Commit broadcast reach both the already-committed replica and that third replica, and emits a canonical commit_propagation_divergence event carrying each replica's committed command plus an all_committed_match flag. The local construction run shows replica 0 NONE (the recoverer's NOOP), replica 1 PUT (the replica that had committed the real command, which ignores the later Commit because its status is already COMMITTED) and replica 2 NONE, so all_committed_match is false: two different committed commands coexist for the same instance after the broadcast rather than the broadcast repairing the disagreement.\\n\\nThe plan now carries three properties on the same unit and obligation: adoption at the resolution, the outcome comparison between the recoverer and the already-committed replica, and agreement across all three replicas after propagation, each with its monitor, identity correlation through the instance, the committed_reply prerequisite as admission alias, and grounding that names the resolution and commit handlers (the third monitor is bound to the resolution binding because that resolution produced the vector being propagated, with the commit handler cited in its grounding instead). A new uncertainty records that the state machines are not executed, so the applied-state consequence stays open. No map object, requirement, premise or earlier observation was changed.\"}"}}
